      "description": "A simple model of a coronal loop in a young star hosting a planet. I used the star DS Tucanae A and its planet as a template for the model. The mass of the planet is less than 14 Earth masses, its age is about 40 millions of years, the distance between the star and the planet is about 17 times the solar radius (which is about 696,000 km). The loop size is derived from the analysis of XMM-Newton observations during flares in X-ray band."
